{"h":3172,"lines":[{"x":0.58925143851344786,"h":0.017441860213405991,"t":"Sample answers for Writing tasks","y":0.045058139655075879,"w":0.31094050089518233,"c":1},{"t":"TEST 3, WRITING TASK 2","w":0.35124760945638023,"h":0.02182431960617004,"y":0.093001261474719654,"c":1,"x":0.084452970619098747},{"x":0.08445297514726538,"y":0.13081395328525658,"w":0.19769673665364582,"h":0.014534884112479496,"c":1,"t":"SAMPLE ANSWER"},{"w":0.675623779296875,"h":0.016122173391104111,"x":0.084452985485525905,"c":1,"y":0.16992433796858686,"t":"This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 5.5 score:"},{"c":1,"w":0.75252517700195309,"h":0.021422589411501103,"t":"I agree with this topic. In my opinion I think that music can join anypeople who has different","x":0.082478455396868738,"y":0.1966854915221925},{"y":0.21941992418145784,"t":"culture together, Music can make a relationship between people all around the world. Although it","h":0.018952168853105467,"c":1,"x":0.084452983895306588,"w":0.79462570190429682},{"w":0.79462570190429671,"h":0.020348836314332486,"c":1,"y":0.23982558184006897,"x":0.082533598086072385,"t":"has different rhytum but when the people who listen to music, their feeling will be better. For the"},{"w":0.77939341227213532,"t":"example the woman who will be mom in the future she can use music to join between mom and","c":1,"y":0.26064367800369503,"x":0.084392684883346572,"h":0.02038441329705909},{"y":0.28341740243506552,"w":0.7984645080566406,"t":"her baby. I have known about how to make the patients feel better and some cases of the patients","h":0.018915510718789275,"c":1,"x":0.082533580795048536},{"c":1,"t":"in the hospital, the doctors will use music for them. When they patients listen to music (solf music)","x":0.082491941063688901,"y":0.3036211155679005,"h":0.020534383093123054,"w":0.81007400512695305},{"t":"it makes them feel better. And now we don't use music only human we can use it with animals and","y":0.32408574972320225,"w":0.80806142171223971,"c":1,"x":0.084452974337381095,"h":0.020491803278688603},{"h":0.019434834488703867,"w":0.090849221547444653,"t":"plants too.","x":0.084133930287101533,"y":0.34784072193683802,"c":1},{"h":0.020491803278688492,"c":1,"y":0.37641866346736808,"w":0.78886754353841138,"x":0.084452984384722457,"t":"Music can make us feel better, although we are different ages, nationalities and culture. when we"},{"c":1,"h":0.023049983521277406,"x":0.08246080589182242,"y":0.39639538014095588,"t":"like the same kind of music. We can join and listen together. One more example I have friend and","w":0.80050999959309888},{"x":0.08253360003371199,"h":0.020491803278688492,"c":1,"y":0.41992433815017183,"t":"he is the foreigner. He is around 25 years old. He likes to go anywhere with me and he likes to","w":0.77159306844075515},{"y":0.43941575312544701,"h":0.026192995819438236,"x":0.08242381712409251,"w":0.77946884155273433,"t":"listen Thai song, especially song for life. He tries to practice to sing Thai song and he can do it.","c":1},{"h":0.018997990919692676,"w":0.28406908671061204,"c":1,"t":"Now he can sing many Thai songs.","y":0.46366279067477767,"x":0.084452980506643099},{"w":0.80806142171223971,"h":0.020348836314332486,"t":"Including I think music has some power to make human's mind. And it can make good relationship","x":0.084452974271600756,"c":1,"y":0.49273255858440423},{"c":1,"x":0.084452963620473914,"y":0.51450189174319871,"w":0.53358927408854162,"t":"between people who has different ages, cultures and nationalities.","h":0.018928340825276946},{"t":"Here is the examiner's comment:","y":0.55232558119491559,"w":0.30710172017415366,"h":0.014534884112479496,"c":1,"x":0.084452978587316582},{"y":0.58858764176576794,"w":0.7466410827636718,"h":0.017654476670870056,"c":1,"t":"The response shows a clear position that is relevant to the task, with examples to","x":0.13051823009732763},{"w":0.7429328918457031,"c":1,"y":0.60576148785223505,"t":"support the main ideas. There is a clear overall progression, with effective use of","h":0.019243506134533517,"x":0.13045883458339555},{"w":0.72936660766601558,"h":0.017496847414880223,"c":1,"t":"cohesive devices [this | them | it] in spite of some errors [For the example | they","x":0.13051823570633947,"y":0.62499999990783184},{"h":0.019893387677840879,"w":0.71796788533528644,"t":"patients | Including \/ In conclusion?]. Paragraphing is adequate. Vocabulary is","x":0.12853890084104383,"y":0.64239590842821959,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.13051823730290057,"t":"generally adequate, but control over spelling and word choice is weak [anypeople |","h":0.017654476670870056,"y":0.66267339224887378,"w":0.76199615478515625},{"y":0.6802325580473666,"c":1,"w":0.75431859334309903,"t":"rhytum | solf \/ soft? | anywhere \/ everywhere? | song for life?], sometimes causing","x":0.130518249273748,"h":0.017441860213405991},{"c":1,"x":0.13046039832150294,"w":0.69684127807617191,"t":"difficulty for the reader. There are attempts at complex sentences, but these","h":0.018957118819670882,"y":0.69906166551147175},{"c":1,"x":0.13044528247744192,"t":"usually contain errors [people who has | Although ... but when], and punctuation is","w":0.76215398152669267,"y":0.71648948352083053,"h":0.021011719336876511},{"w":0.76391555786132814,"y":0.73546511639821666,"t":"sometimes faulty (incorrect capitalisation, misuse of commas and full stops). Better","c":1,"h":0.017441860213405991,"x":0.13051822881331929},{"x":0.13051822257254647,"y":0.75436046523586031,"c":1,"w":0.73704416910807291,"h":0.017441860213405991,"t":"control over spelling, grammar and punctuation might improve the overall score."},{"c":1,"w":0.036468331019083644,"t":"133","x":0.86564299369817832,"y":0.95203488362865729,"h":0.013081395460708523}],"w":2400}